      "order_index": 1,
      "content_text": "# Parts of Speech (basic)\n\n**Level**: Class 8 | **Topic**: Parts of Speech (পদ প্রকরণ / শব্দশ্রেণি)\n\n\n## 1. 📖 Grammar Rules & Explanations (নিয়মাবলী ও ব্যাখ্যা)\n\n- **Noun:** A word that names a person, place, thing, or idea. Example: boy, city.\n\n- **Pronoun:** A word used in place of a noun. Example: he, she, it.\n\n- **Verb:** A word that expresses action or state. Example: run, is.\n\n- **Adjective:** A word that describes a noun. Example: big, blue.\n\n- **Adverb:** A word that describes a verb, adjective, or adverb. Example: quickly, very.\n\n- **Preposition:** A word that shows relationship. Example: in, on, at.\n\n- **Conjunction:** A word that connects clauses. Example: and, but, or.\n\n- **Interjection:** A word that expresses emotion. Example: wow, oh.\n\n\n## 2. 💡 Practical Examples (বাস্তব উদাহরণসমূহ)\n\n1. The boy plays in the park. (boy - noun, plays - verb, park - noun)\n\n2. She gave it to him. (She - pronoun, it - pronoun, him - pronoun)\n\n3. They are running fast. (are - verb, running - verb)\n\n4. The big red apple is sweet. (big - adjective, red - adjective, sweet - adjective)\n\n5. He runs very quickly. (very - adverb, quickly - adverb)\n\n6. The book is on the table. (on - preposition)\n\n7. I like tea and coffee. (and - conjunction)\n\n8. Wow! What a surprise! (Wow - interjection)\n\n\n## 3. ✍️ Practice Drills (অনুশীলনমূলক কাজ)\n\n- **Exercise 1:** Identify the nouns in: The teacher teaches students.\n\n- **Exercise 2:** Find pronouns in: He gave her the book.\n\n- **Exercise 3:** Underline verbs in: Birds fly in the sky.\n\n- **Exercise 4:** Circle adjectives in: The tall man wears a black hat.\n\n- **Exercise 5:** Identify adverbs in: She sings beautifully.\n\n- **Exercise 6:** Find prepositions in: The cat is under the chair.\n\n- **Exercise 7:** Spot conjunctions in: I study but play games.\n\n- **Exercise 8:** Find interjections in: Oh! I forgot my keys.\n\n- **Exercise 9:** Find out parts of speech from any sentences.",
