      "order_index": 1,
      "content_text": "# Tense (simple)\n\n**Level**: Class 8 | **Topic**: Tense (কাল ও সময় - প্রাথমিক)\n\n\n## 1. 📖 Grammar Rules & Explanations (নিয়মাবলী ও ব্যাখ্যা)\n\n- **PRESENT TENSE\nSimple Present:** subject + base verb. Habits and truths. Structure: She reads. Example: Birds fly south in winter.\n\n- **More examples:** Water boils at 100°C. / She speaks Arabic fluently. / The sun rises in the east. / We visit the Grand Mosque every Friday. / Coffee wakes me up in the morning.\n\n- **Present Continuous:** subject + am/is/are + verb-ing. Actions happening now. Structure: She is reading. Example: He is studying mathematics right now.\n\n- **More examples:** It is raining heavily outside. / They are playing football in the park. / I am cooking majboos for dinner. / She is driving to Seeb right now. / The kids are watching cartoons.\n\n- **Present Perfect:** subject + have/has + past participle. Started in past, continues now or has relevance now. Structure: She has read. Example: I have lived here for 5 years.\n\n- **More examples:** We have just finished lunch. / She has visited Nizwa Fort twice. / They have lost their keys again. / I have never tried Omani halwa before. / He has already left for the airport.\n\n- **Present Perfect Continuous:** subject + have/has been + verb-ing. Action started before now, still happening or recently stopped (focus on duration). Structure: She has been reading. Example: They have been waiting for an hour.\n\n- **More examples:** It has been raining since morning. / She has been learning Arabic for six months. / We have been walking around Muttrah Souq all afternoon. / He has been feeling tired lately. / The workers have been repairing the road for weeks.\n\n- **PAST TENSE\nSimple Past:** subject + past form. Completed action at definite time. Structure: She read. Example: We visited the museum yesterday.\n\n- **More examples:** I bought dates from the market last week. / They watched the sunset at Qurum Beach. / She called me yesterday evening. / He finished his homework early. / We celebrated Eid with family.\n\n- **Past Continuous:** subject + was/were + verb-ing. Action happening at a specific past time (often interrupted). Structure: She was reading. Example: I was sleeping when the phone rang.\n\n- **More examples:** We were driving to Muscat when it started raining. / She was cooking when the power went out. / They were playing in the garden at 5 pm. / He was working late last night. / I was waiting for the bus at the stop.\n\n- **Past Perfect:** subject + had + past participle. One past action before another past action. Structure: She had read. Example: He had finished dinner before she arrived.\n\n- **More examples:** They had left before the storm began. / She had already eaten when I invited her. / We had visited the wadi before we went to the beach. / By the time we arrived, the shop had closed. / He had studied English before he moved to Oman.\n\n- **Past Perfect Continuous:** subject + had been + verb-ing. Action in progress before another past action (emphasis on duration). Structure: She had been reading. Example: They had been playing for two hours when it started raining.\n\n- **More examples:** She had been waiting for the taxi for 30 minutes when it finally came. / We had been walking in the heat for hours before we found shade. / He had been working all day, so he was exhausted. / They had been arguing for a long time before they made up. / I had been living in Muscat for three years before I learned some Dhofari words.\n\n- **FUTURE TENSE\nSimple Future:** subject + will + base verb. Planned or predicted action. Structure: She will read. Example: We will go to the beach tomorrow.\n\n- **More examples:** I will call you later tonight. / She will travel to Salalah next month. / It will be very hot tomorrow. / They will finish the project soon. / We will meet at the café after work.\n\n- **Future Continuous:** subject + will be + verb-ing. Action that will be happening at a specific future time. Structure: She will be reading. Example: I will be working when you arrive.\n\n- **More examples:** At 8 pm, we will be having dinner. / She will be studying at the library tomorrow afternoon. / They will be flying to Dubai this time next week. / I will be driving to Nizwa around noon. / He will be waiting for us at the gate.\n\n- **Future Perfect:** subject + will have + past participle. Action that will be completed before a future time. Structure: She will have read. Example: By next year, she will have completed her studies.\n\n- **More examples:** By Ramadan, we will have saved enough money for a trip. / She will have arrived home by the time you call. / They will have finished the construction by December. / I will have learned 200 Arabic words by the end of the course. / He will have eaten breakfast before 7 am.\n\n- **Future Perfect Continuous:** subject + will have been + verb-ing. Action in progress up to a future time (emphasis on duration). Structure: She will have been reading. Example: By evening, they will have been working for 8 hours.\n\n- **More examples:** By next summer, she will have been living in Oman for ten years. / By the time the flight lands, we will have been traveling for 12 hours. / They will have been waiting for over an hour by then. / I will have been studying English for two years by December. / He will have been driving for six hours when he reaches Salalah.\n\n\n## 2. 💡 Practical Examples (বাস্তব উদাহরণসমূহ)\n\n1. Simple Present: The teacher teaches English every day.\n\n2. Present Continuous: The students are writing a test now.\n\n3. Present Perfect: I have completed my homework.\n\n4. Present Perfect Continuous: We have been learning English for 3 years.\n\n5. Simple Past: She went to the market yesterday.\n\n6. Past Continuous: While I was reading, the doorbell rang.\n\n7. Past Perfect: He had finished his meal before we arrived.\n\n8. Past Perfect Continuous: They had been walking for hours when they found shelter.\n\n9. Simple Future: You will get the result next week.\n\n10. Future Continuous: At 8 pm tomorrow, I will be watching a movie.\n\n11. Future Perfect: By 2026, she will have graduated from university.\n\n12. Future Perfect Continuous: By June, they will have been working here for 5 years.\n\n\n## 3. ✍️ Practice Drills (অনুশীলনমূলক কাজ)\n\n- **Exercise 1:** Convert to present continuous: She (read) a book.\n\n- **Exercise 2:** Convert to simple past: They (play) cricket yesterday.\n\n- **Exercise 3:** Convert to present perfect: I (finish) my work.\n\n- **Exercise 4:** Convert to past continuous: While he (study), the phone rang.\n\n- **Exercise 5:** Convert to simple future: We (meet) you after class.\n\n- **Exercise 6:** Convert to future continuous: At 3 pm, I (do) my homework.",
