      "order_index": 1,
      "content_text": "# Subject–Verb Agreement (basic)\n\n**Level**: Class 8 | **Topic**: Subject–Verb Agreement (basic)\n\n\n## 1. 📖 Grammar Rules & Explanations (নিয়মাবলী ও ব্যাখ্যা)\n\n- **THIRD PERSON SINGULAR RULE\nIn present tense, 3rd person singular (he, she, it, singular noun) adds -s or -es to the base verb.\nExample:** He walks / She plays / It runs.\n\n- **Add -s to most verbs for 3rd person singular.\nExamples:** speak → speaks, read → reads, love → loves, work → works, help → helps.\n\n- **Add -es to verbs ending in s, x, z, ch, sh for 3rd person singular.\nExamples:** pass → passes, mix → mixes, buzz → buzzes, catch → catches, wash → washes.\n\n- **Verbs ending in consonant + y change y to i and add -es. Verbs ending in vowel + y just add -s.\nExamples:** try → tries, cry → cries, study → studies, play → plays, stay → stays.\n\n- **GENERAL SVA RULES\nSingular subjects take singular verbs; plural subjects take plural verbs.\nExample:** The dog barks / The dogs bark. / He reads / They read.\n\n- **Use 'is' with singular nouns and 3rd person singular pronouns (he, she, it); use 'are' with plural nouns and pronouns (I, you, we, they).\nExample:** She is busy / They are busy / The book is new / The books are new.\n\n- **Collective nouns (team, group, family, class, committee) are usually singular and take singular verbs.\nExample:** The team is winning / The class is studying / The family has gathered.\n\n- **Singular indefinite pronouns—everyone, everybody, someone, somebody, anyone, anybody, each, either, neither, nothing—take singular verbs.\nExample:** Everyone is ready / Somebody has lost their keys / Each student gets a certificate.\n\n- **Compound subjects joined by 'and' usually take plural verbs (treat as multiple).\nExample:** Ram and Sita are friends / The teacher and students are happy.\n\n- **Subjects joined by 'or' or 'nor' take a verb that agrees with the nearest (closest) subject.\nExample:** Either you or he is coming / Neither she nor they are present / The boys or the girl has the answer.\n\n- **Uncountable nouns (water, milk, sand, information, advice, luggage, furniture) take singular verbs even though they may seem plural.\nExample:** Water is essential / The advice is helpful / Your luggage has arrived.\n\n- **Words like 'news', 'mathematics', 'physics', 'economics' are singular despite ending in 's'.\nExample:** The news is shocking / Mathematics is difficult / Physics has many theories.\n\n\n## 2. 💡 Practical Examples (বাস্তব উদাহরণসমূহ)\n\n1. 3rd person singular +s: He plays / She reads / It runs / The dog barks.\n\n2. 3rd person singular +es (s,x,z,ch,sh): He passes / She mixes / It buzzes / He catches.\n\n3. Consonant + y → i + es: He tries / She studies / The child cries.\n\n4. Vowel + y just +s: She plays / He stays / The child prays.\n\n5. Singular vs Plural: The boy plays (singular) / The boys play (plural).\n\n6. Collective nouns: The team is winning / The class has finished / The committee is meeting.\n\n7. Singular indefinites: Everyone is ready / Someone has arrived / Neither child is ready.\n\n8. Compound (and): Ram and Sita are friends / The teacher and students are happy.\n\n9. Compound (or/nor nearest rule): Either you or he is coming / The boys or the girl has the answer.\n\n10. Uncountable (singular verb): Water is essential / The advice is helpful / News is important.\n\n11. With 'there is/are': There is a book / There are books / There is a cat / There are cats.\n\n12. Regular verbs 3rd singular: speak → speaks / help → helps / work → works / read → reads.\n\n13. Irregular verb 'be': I am / He is / She is / You are / They are / We are.\n\n14. Irregular verb 'have': He has / She has / They have / I have / You have.\n\n15. Irregular verb 'go': He goes / She goes / I go / They go.\n\n16. Irregular verb 'do': He does / She does / I do / You do / We do / They do.\n\n\n## 3. ✍️ Practice Drills (অনুশীলনমূলক কাজ)\n\n- **Exercise 1:** Complete: She _____ (play) tennis every day.\n\n- **Exercise 2:** Complete: The cat _____ (jump) on the wall.\n\n- **Exercise 3:** Complete: He _____ (study) hard for exams.\n\n- **Exercise 4:** Complete: She _____ (cry) when she is sad.\n\n- **Exercise 5:** Complete: He _____ (pass) the test easily.\n\n- **Exercise 6:** Complete: The dog _____ (barks/bark) at the door.\n\n- **Exercise 7:** Fix error: He go to school every day.\n\n- **Exercise 8:** Fix error: She do not like milk.\n\n- **Exercise 9:** Fix error: The team are winning.\n\n- **Exercise 10:** Choose: Either of them _____ (is/are) correct.",
