      "content_text": "# Narration (statements)\n\n**Level**: Class 8 | **Topic**: Narration (উক্তি পরিবর্তন: উক্তি ও বর্ণনা)\n\n\n## 1. 📖 Grammar Rules & Explanations (নিয়মাবলী ও ব্যাখ্যা)\n\n- **DIRECT SPEECH:** Reports exact words spoken using quotation marks.\nStructure: Subject + reporting verb + exact words.\nExample: She said, 'I am happy.'\nThe speaker quotes the exact words said.\n\n- **INDIRECT SPEECH (Reported Speech):** Reports what someone said without exact words.\nStructure: Subject + reporting verb + that + indirect statement.\nExample: She said that she was happy.\nMeaning is conveyed without direct quotes.\n\n- **COMMON REPORTING VERBS:** said, told, informed, mentioned, remarked, declared, stated, claimed, announced, suggested, replied, answered, explained.\nExample: He said / He told me / He informed us / He declared / He announced\n\n- **TENSE CHANGES IN INDIRECT SPEECH\nSimple Present becomes Simple Past:** I like tea becomes He said that he liked tea.\nPresent Continuous becomes Past Continuous: I am reading becomes She said that she was reading.\nSimple Past becomes Past Perfect: I went yesterday becomes He said that he had gone the day before.\nPresent Perfect becomes Past Perfect: I have finished becomes She said that she had finished.\n\n- **NO TENSE CHANGE IN CERTAIN CASES\nIf reporting verb is in present tense:** She says, 'I am happy' becomes She says that she is happy.\nUniversal truths: He said, 'Water boils at 100 degrees' becomes He said that water boils at 100 degrees.\n\n- **PRONOUN CHANGES IN INDIRECT SPEECH\n1st person (I, we) becomes 3rd person (he/she, they)\nExample:** I am ready becomes He said that he was ready.\n2nd person (you) may change: You are late becomes She told me that I was late.\n\n- **TIME EXPRESSION CHANGES:** today becomes that day, tomorrow becomes the next day, yesterday becomes the day before, now becomes then, last week becomes the week before, next month becomes the following month.\nExample: I will come tomorrow becomes He said that he would come the next day.\n\n- **PLACE EXPRESSION CHANGES:** here becomes there, this becomes that, these becomes those.\nExample: I am here becomes He said that he was there.\nExample: This book is mine becomes She said that that book was hers.\n\n- **TENSE PATTERNS:** Present to Past, Present Continuous to Past Continuous, Present Perfect to Past Perfect, will to would, Past to Past Perfect, Past Continuous to Past Perfect Continuous.\n\n- **CONVERTING AFFIRMATIVE STATEMENTS\nDirect:** I am a doctor (He said) becomes Indirect: He said that he was a doctor.\nDirect: She loves music (They said) becomes Indirect: They said that she loved music.\nDirect: We have finished work (He said) becomes Indirect: He said that they had finished the work.\n\n- **CONVERTING NEGATIVE STATEMENTS\nDirect:** I do not like coffee (She said) becomes Indirect: She said that she did not like coffee.\nDirect: He will not come (She said) becomes Indirect: She said that he would not come.\nThe negative structure remains in indirect speech.\n\n- **REPORTING WITH TOLD vs SAID\nWith SAID:** He said that...\nWith TOLD: He told me that... (Must have indirect object)\nUse told when the listener is important or mentioned.\n\n\n## 2. 💡 Practical Examples (বাস্তব উদাহরণসমূহ)\n\n1. Simple Present: I read books becomes He said that he read books.\n\n2. Present Continuous: I am cooking becomes She said that she was cooking.\n\n3. Present Perfect: I have eaten becomes He said that he had eaten.\n\n4. Simple Past: I went to school becomes She said that she had gone to school.\n\n5. Simple Future: I will help becomes He said that he would help.\n\n6. With told: I am ready becomes She told me that she was ready.\n\n7. Negative: I don't like tea becomes She said that she didn't like tea.\n\n8. Time change: I came today becomes He said that he had come that day.\n\n9. Place change: I am here becomes She said that she was there.\n\n10. Universal truth: The sun rises in the east becomes He said that the sun rises in the east.\n\n11. Pronoun change: We are ready becomes They said that they were ready.\n\n12. Multiple changes: I will come tomorrow becomes He said that he would come the next day.\n\n\n## 3. ✍️ Practice Drills (অনুশীলনমূলক কাজ)\n\n- **Exercise 1:** Convert: I like music (She said) to indirect.\n\n- **Exercise 2:** Convert: I am studying (He said) to indirect.\n\n- **Exercise 3:** Convert: I will help you (He said) to indirect.\n\n- **Exercise 4:** Convert: I went to Delhi yesterday (She said) to indirect.\n\n- **Exercise 5:** Convert: I do not like coffee (He said) to indirect.\n\n- **Exercise 6:** Convert with told: You are late (She told him) to indirect.\n\n- **Exercise 7:** Change time: I will come tomorrow (He said) with time change.\n\n- **Exercise 8:** Change place: I am here (She said) with place change.\n\n- **Exercise 9:** Universal truth: Water boils at 100 degrees (Teacher said) to indirect.\n\n- **Exercise 10:** Negative statement: They don't speak English (He said) to indirect.",
