      "order_index": 1,
      "content_text": "# Parts of Speech (word form)\n\n**Level**: Class 9-10 | **Topic**: Parts of Speech: Word Forms (শব্দের রূপান্তর)\n\n\n## 1. 📖 Grammar Rules & Explanations (নিয়মাবলী ও ব্যাখ্যা)\n\n- **Word form:** the same root word can change into noun, verb, adjective, or adverb.\nExample: educate → education (noun), educate (verb), educational (adjective), educationally (adverb).\n\n- **Noun forms:** add -tion/-sion (educate → education, decide → decision), -ment (develop → development), -ness (happy → happiness), -ity (active → activity), -ance/-ence (perform → performance, differ → difference).\n\n- **Verb forms:** add -ize/-ise (modern → modernize), -ify (class → classify), -en (strength → strengthen).\n\n- **Adjective forms:** add -ful (help → helpful), -less (hope → hopeless), -able/-ible (comfort → comfortable, access → accessible), -ive (create → creative), -al (nation → national), -ic (music → musical).\n\n- **Adverb forms:** adjective + -ly (quick → quickly, careful → carefully).\nExceptions: good → well, fast → fast, hard → hard.\n\n- **Common suffix changes:** beauty → beautiful → beautifully; success → successful → successfully; courage → courageous → courageously.\n\n\n## 2. 💡 Practical Examples (বাস্তব উদাহরণসমূহ)\n\n1. educate (verb) → education (noun) → educational (adjective) → educationally (adverb)\n\n2. decide (verb) → decision (noun) → decisive (adjective) → decisively (adverb)\n\n3. create (verb) → creation (noun) → creative (adjective) → creatively (adverb)\n\n4. beauty (noun) → beautiful (adjective) → beautifully (adverb)\n\n5. success (noun) → succeed (verb) → successful (adjective) → successfully (adverb)\n\n6. strength (noun) → strengthen (verb) → strong (adjective) → strongly (adverb)\n\n7. help (verb) → help (noun) → helpful (adjective) → helpfully (adverb)\n\n8. care (noun/verb) → careful (adjective) → carefully (adverb)\n\n\n## 3. ✍️ Practice Drills (অনুশীলনমূলক কাজ)\n\n- **Exercise 1:** Change to noun: improve, decide, educate, develop, prepare.\n\n- **Exercise 2:** Change to adjective: beauty, danger, comfort, nature, create.\n\n- **Exercise 3:** Change to adverb: quick, careful, slow, polite, clear.\n\n- **Exercise 4:** Give all forms (noun/verb/adj/adv): success, courage, peace, difference, honesty.\n\n- **Exercise 5:** Choose correct form: She spoke ___ (confident/confidently).\n\n- **Exercise 6:** Choose correct form: The ___ (decision/decide) was final.",
