      "content_text": "# Tense\n\n**Level**: Class 9-10 | **Topic**: Tense: All Tenses & Structures (সমগ্র কাল ও গঠন)\n\n\n## 1. 📖 Grammar Rules & Explanations (নিয়মাবলী ও ব্যাখ্যা)\n\n- **Continuous tenses show actions in progress. Structure:** be + verb-ing.\n\n- **Simple tenses show routine, facts, or completed actions. Structure:** Base verb / V2 / will + base verb.\n\n- **Simple present:** base verb (s/es with he/she/it). Use for habits and facts.\n\n- **Simple past:** V2. Use for completed actions in the past.\n\n- **Simple future:** will + base verb. Use for future actions or decisions.\n\n- **Present continuous:** am/is/are + verb-ing. Use for actions happening now or temporary actions.\n\n- **Past continuous:** was/were + verb-ing. Use for actions in progress at a specific past time.\n\n- **Future continuous:** will be + verb-ing. Use for actions that will be in progress at a future time.\n\n- **Perfect tenses show completion. Structure:** have/has/had + past participle (V3).\n\n- **Present perfect:** has/have + V3. Use for completed actions with result now or life experience.\n\n- **Past perfect:** had + V3. Use for the earlier of two past actions.\n\n- **Perfect continuous:** has/have been + verb-ing or had been + verb-ing to show duration.\n\n- **Present perfect continuous:** has/have been + verb-ing. Use for actions started in the past and continuing now.\n\n- **Past perfect continuous:** had been + verb-ing. Use for actions that continued up to a past time.\n\n\n## 2. 💡 Practical Examples (বাস্তব উদাহরণসমূহ)\n\n1. Simple present: She reads every day.\n\n2. Simple past: He visited Dhaka last week.\n\n3. Simple future: They will start tomorrow.\n\n4. Present continuous: I am reading a book now.\n\n5. Past continuous: I was reading at 7 p.m.\n\n6. Future continuous: I will be reading at 9 p.m.\n\n7. Present perfect: She has finished her homework.\n\n8. Past perfect: They had left before the rain started.\n\n9. Present perfect continuous: He has been studying for two hours.\n\n10. Past perfect continuous: She had been waiting for a long time.\n\n11. Past vs. past continuous: I was cooking when the doorbell rang.\n\n\n## 3. ✍️ Practice Drills (অনুশীলনমূলক কাজ)\n\n- **Exercise 1:** Convert to simple present: She is playing now.\n\n- **Exercise 2:** Convert to simple past: He is cooking dinner.\n\n- **Exercise 3:** Make a simple future sentence with 'tomorrow'.\n\n- **Exercise 4:** Convert to present continuous: He plays football.\n\n- **Exercise 5:** Convert to past continuous: They watch TV.\n\n- **Exercise 6:** Fill in: She ___ (study) for her test right now.\n\n- **Exercise 7:** Choose the correct tense: I ___ (finish) my work already.\n\n- **Exercise 8:** Rewrite using past perfect: The train left, then we arrived.\n\n- **Exercise 9:** Make a sentence in future continuous with 'at 8 p.m.'.\n\n- **Exercise 10:** Fill in: They ___ (play) since morning.\n\n- **Exercise 11:** Identify the tense: She had been waiting for an hour.",
