        "Misplaced Modifiers: A modifier placed too far from the word it describes, causing confusion.\nWrong: Running quickly, the tree seemed to move. (Tree is not running!)\nCorrect: Running quickly, the student dodged the tree.\nWrong: I bought a saree from my friend with a torn edge. (Friend doesn't have torn edge)\nCorrect: I bought a saree with a torn edge from my friend.\n💡 Place the modifier CLOSE to the word it describes!",
