        "Zero Article (No Article): Used with plural countable nouns and uncountable nouns when speaking generally.\nGeneral Truth: Students need education. (all students, not specific)\nCountries: Bangladesh is beautiful. (but: The United Kingdom)\nMeals: I eat breakfast at 7 AM. (but: The breakfast was delicious - specific)\nSubjects: She studies mathematics. (but: The mathematics in HSC is challenging)\n💡 HSC Tip: Zero article = general meaning!",
